2:T803,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is Klondike Solitaire?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Klondike is the layout most people picture when they hear \"solitaire\": seven tableau columns, a stock pile, and four foundations built by suit from Ace to King. It shipped with Windows in 1990 and has been the default computer card game ever since."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can every Klondike game be won?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Roughly 79% of Klondike deals are theoretically solvable, but face-down cards hide information you need, so real win rates run far lower â€” winning about a third of your Turn 1 games is a solid result."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between Turn 1 and Turn 3?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Turn 1 flips one stock card at a time, so every card becomes reachable in order. Turn 3 flips three at once with only the top card playable, burying two cards per group. Here, Easy plays Turn 1 with unlimited stock passes, Medium caps Turn 1 at three passes, and Hard is Turn 3 with three passes."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I move multiple cards at once?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Pick any face-up card in a column and everything stacked on top of it travels together. Drop the group on a card one rank higher in the opposite color â€” a red 9 onto a black 10, for example."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens when the stock pile is empty?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Click the empty stock spot to turn the waste pile back over and keep drawing. On Easy you can cycle the stock forever; Medium and Hard allow three passes total, so make each trip through count."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is this game free to play?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Klondike here costs nothing and never will â€” no account, no install, unlimited fresh deals, and your undo history, timer, and win statistics all live right in your browser."}}]}f:X
